course: dictionary
lesson: 2101
title: Contour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A contour is the shape or outline of something, especially its curves. On a map, a contour line joins places that are the same height above sea level. «Contour lines join points of equal height above sea level.» So every line on the map marks one height.
explain: Look at how the lines sit together. «Lines drawn close together mean the ground is steep.» Lines far apart mean gentle ground. Reading the spacing tells you what the land is like before you ever walk on it.
explain: Contour can also be a verb, meaning to shape something to fit a curve. Context helps you tell the two apart. In «A key explains the symbols, contour lines show how high and steep the land is», contour lines is a noun phrase: a kind of line on a map.
fact: Contour means the outline or shape of something, such as the contour of a face or a coastline.
fact: A contour line on a map joins places that are the same height above sea level.
fact: Lines close together on a map mean a steep slope; lines far apart mean gentle ground.
fact: In art, contour drawing traces the outline of an object.
fact: As a verb, to contour means to shape something to fit a curve.
exercise: «Lines drawn close together mean the ground is steep.» On a map, what do close contour lines show? | Sea level | Gentle ground | A river | *A steep slope
exercise: «Contour lines join points of equal height above sea level.» What does a contour line join? | Places with the same colour grass | Places in the sea only | *Places that are the same height | Places that are far apart
exercise: «A key explains the symbols, contour lines show how high and steep the land is, and grid references let two people point to exactly the same square.» Find and copy the phrase that names lines on a map showing height. | symbols | *contour lines | key | grid references
test: «The contour of the coastline was rough and jagged.» What does contour mean here? | *The outline or shape | The height above sea level | A type of map key | A kind of paint
test: On a map, lines far apart mean what kind of ground? | Underwater ground | *Gentle ground | Ground with rivers | Steep ground
exam: «Contour lines show how high and steep the land is.» On a map, what do contour lines show? | Where the sea meets the land | *How high and how steep the land is | The names of the towns | The colour of the grass
